From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apps_mem: log map requests, pass remote heap ones to the kernel

Once the ADSP's audio PD is created (-a audiopd) it asks apps_mem for
memory with flags other than ADSP_MMAP_ADD_PAGES, and every such request
was rejected as a "DMA buffer request" without saying what it was. Log
the heap id, flags, address and length of every request, and hand
ADSP_MMAP_REMOTE_HEAP_ADDR requests to FASTRPC_IOCTL_MMAP, which the
kernel serves from the channel's remote heap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/apps_mem.c b/hexagonrpcd/apps_mem.c
index f4d0bf9..442a4d2 100644
--- a/hexagonrpcd/apps_mem.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/apps_mem.c
@@ -60,7 +60,20 @@ static uint32_t apps_mem_request_map64(void *data,
 	struct fastrpc_req_mmap mmap;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!(first_in->rflags & ADSP_MMAP_ADD_PAGES)) {
+	/*
+	 * Say what the DSP asked for: the static audio PD makes requests this
+	 * daemon does not serve, and what to add depends on these values.
+	 */
+	fprintf(stderr, "apps_mem_request_map64: heap %u lflags 0x%x rflags 0x%x vin 0x%" PRIx64 " len 0x%" PRIx64 "\n",
+		first_in->heap_id, first_in->lflags, first_in->rflags,
+		first_in->vin, first_in->len);
+
+	/*
+	 * Memory for a static PD's remote heap: the kernel allocates it from
+	 * the channel's memory-region and assigns it to the DSP's VMs.
+	 */
+	if (first_in->rflags != ADSP_MMAP_REMOTE_HEAP_ADDR &&
+	    !(first_in->rflags & ADSP_MMAP_ADD_PAGES)) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "Unsupported mmap operation: DMA buffer request\n");
 		return AEE_EUNSUPPORTED;
 	}
